(-T) commands ->
1.-T0 slow 
~scans one port at a time and waits 5 minutes between sending each probe.
2.-T1 sneaky
~ is often used during real engagements where stealth is more important.
3.-T2 polite
~used for normal scan where stealth is a bit compromised.
4.-T3 normal 
~jsut normal
5.-T4 aggerasive
~it is often used during CTFs and when learning to scan on practice targets.
6.-T5 insane
~is the most aggressive in terms of speed; however, 
~this can affect the accuracy of the scan results due to the increased likelihood of packet loss

